Export all three compat getusershell functions from libsudo_util.

On a system without getusershell() (QNX), sudo builds its own
setusershell/getusershell/endusershell into libsudo_util as sudo_*, but
configure adds only sudo_getusershell to the library's export list. The
sudoers plugin and visudo call the other two, so linking them fails with
"undefined reference to sudo_setusershell" / "sudo_endusershell".

configure is changed along with configure.ac so the release tarball builds
without regenerating it.

Upstream-Status: Pending (affects any system without getusershell())

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2768,7 +2768,7 @@
     AC_CHECK_DECLS([getusershell])
 ], [
     AC_LIBOBJ(getusershell)
-    SUDO_APPEND_COMPAT_EXP(sudo_getusershell)
+    SUDO_APPEND_COMPAT_EXP(sudo_getusershell sudo_setusershell sudo_endusershell)
 ])
 AC_CHECK_FUNCS([reallocarray], [], [
     AC_LIBOBJ(reallocarray)
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -23028,7 +23028,7 @@
 esac
 
 
-    for _sym in sudo_getusershell; do
+    for _sym in sudo_getusershell sudo_setusershell sudo_endusershell; do
 	COMPAT_EXP="${COMPAT_EXP}${_sym}
 "
     done
